  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Deep-dive into opportunities for private sector engagement in water treatment and re-use in Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to identify commercially viable investment opportunities for Dutch water technology providers in Bangladesh through three targeted market studies. These include: 1.	Water supply and treatment in economic zones,2.	Municipal sewage management opportunities, and3.	Business-to-business (B2B) prospects in the ready-made garment (RMG) industry. The project supports the broader transition in bilateral cooperation from aid to trade by informing strategic Dutch private sector engagement in Bangladesh&apos;s water sector, in alignment with government priorities and potential Public-Private Partnerships (PPPs). It is implemented in cooperation with the Netherlands embassy in Dhaka and the Partners for Water programme.</narrative>
  </description>
